ver at the Olympics for that nation. The bronze medal went to the Danish pair of " [:a {:href "/athletes/93965"} "Michael Maze"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/93966"} "Finn Tugwell"] ", the only non-Asian medal in table tennis at the 2004 Olympics. The second Chinese team, Kong Linghui and Wang Hao, were surprisingly eliminated in the round of 16 by the Swedish team of " [:a {:href "/athletes/2637"} "Jan-Ove Waldner"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/2632"} "Jörgen Persson"] "."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "People's Republic of China 1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CHN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CHN.png"}] "CHN"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "8"} [:a {:href "/athletes/109572"} "Chen Qi"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/107523"} "Ma Lin"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} "Hong Kong, China 2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/HKG"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/HKG.png"}] "HKG"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "8"} [:a {:href "/athletes/107499"} "Ko Lai Chak"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/107520"} "Li Ching"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} "Denmark"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/DEN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/DEN.png"}] "DEN"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "8"} [:a {:href "/athletes/93965"} "Michael Maze"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/939